### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension. Also copy these into Postman/Thunder Client.

### Health check
GET http://localhost:3000/api/health

### GET all
GET http://localhost:3000/api/requests

### GET all, filtered
GET http://localhost:3000/api/requests?status=open

### GET one
GET http://localhost:3000/api/requests/1

### POST - create (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requesterName": "Thandi",
  "title": "Broken light",
  "description": "Hallway light does not turn on.",
  "category": "Electrical",
  "priority": "high"
}

### POST - invalid (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "" }

### PUT - replace (expect 200)
PUT http://localhost:3000/api/requests/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requesterName": "Sample User",
  "title": "Leaking tap (updated)",
  "description": "Now also dripping under the sink.",
  "category": "Plumbing",
  "priority": "high",
  "status": "in-progress"
}

### PATCH - partial update (expect 200)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/requests/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "resolved" }

### DELETE (expect 204)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/requests/1

### GET missing (expect 404)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/requests/999
